    <div class="body">
      <div class="rail">Gesture</div>
      <div class="flow">
        <p>
          <strong>Track the gesture, don't detect it.</strong> A discrete "swipe recognised →
          expand" still feels like a trigger; following the finger and snapping is what reads as
          intentional. The codebase already has this idiom in three drag sheets —
          <code>transactions.tsx:512</code>, <code>property-analytics.tsx:309</code>,
          <code>trades-analytics.tsx:317</code> — pointer events plus <code>touch-action: none</code>
