        </p>
        <pre><code>pointerdown on the handle → capture, record y0, dragging = true, transition off
pointermove               → dy = y0 - y;  progress = clamp(dy / 56, 0, 1)
                            rubber-band past 1.0; abort if |dx| &gt; |dy|
pointerup / cancel        → progress &gt; 0.45 (or velocity &gt; 0.4 px/ms) ? expand : settle closed</code></pre>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Shrink the hit area</strong> from 320 × 44 to about 120 × 36, centred on the handle. That alone kills "it pops up if you touch it".</li>
          <li><strong><code>touch-action: none</code> on the handle only</strong> — never the full-width strip, or a page scroll starting near the bottom edge gets eaten.</li>
